expression: text
---
Add a source to an environment; a later source wins over an earlier one

Usage: kagebunshin project add-source [OPTIONS] --provider <PROVIDER> <PROJECT> <ENV>

Arguments:
  <PROJECT>  The project
  <ENV>      The environment

Options:
      --json                 Print machine-readable JSON; errors go to stderr as JSON
      --provider <PROVIDER>  Where the values come from: AWS Secrets Manager, the local store or Proton Pass [possible values: aws_sm, file, proton]
      --prefix <PREFIX>      Read every secret whose name starts with this
      --socket <PATH>        Daemon socket [default: $KAGEBUNSHIN_SOCKET, else a per-user runtime dir]
      --env <ENV>            Environment to use instead of the project's default
      --secret <NAME>        Read one secret (for file: a store section, e.g. widget.dev; for proton: vault/KEY); repeat to read several, a later one winning a key two set
      --key <KEY>            The secret's whole string is this key's value, not a JSON object (for proton: rename the key); takes exactly one --secret
      --project <NAME>       Project to use instead of the one for this folder; it must claim this checkout's remotes
      --profile <PROFILE>    aws_sm only: the AWS profile for this source
      --region <REGION>      aws_sm only: the AWS region for this source
      --optional             If the source fails, resolve the environment without it
  -h, --help                 Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version              Print version
